<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n56998" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεφᾰλ-ικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>for the head</i>, of remedies, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. ἔμπλαστροι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					3.88
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Asclep.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.543
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυνάμεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					3.48
				</span></i>
			 (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεφαλαλγικαῖς</span>
			), cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Arch.Pap.</u>
				4.270
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέλτοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					2.607
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κεφαλική, ἡ</span>, name of a herb, Griffith &lt;*&gt;
			Thompson <i>Demotic Magical Papyrus</i> verso<i><span class="en">
				iv 10
			</span></i>. Adv. -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς</span>”
				<i>after the manner of a head,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Corp.Herm.
					10.11
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>touching the head</i> or <i>life</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πράγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PMag.Leid.V.</u>
					5.13
				</span></i>
			; <i>capital</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δίκη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>POxy.</u>
					2104.15
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii A.D.)</span>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμωρία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Rev.Bibl.</u>
					35.285
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Jerusalem</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cod.Just.</u>
				1.12.3.2
			</span></i> (Theodosius II), <i><span class="en">
				Just.
				<u>Nou.</u>
				85.3.1
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κίνδυνος</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				123.31
			</span></i>. Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κῶς,
			κολασθήσεσθαι</span> to be punished <i>capitally</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdn.
				2.13.9
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμωρεῖσθαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Just.
					<u>Nou.</u>
					123.31
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cod.Just.</u>
				9.4.6.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>belonging to an individual</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μερίς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PMasp.</u>
					151.89
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(vi A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. σμίλη</span>
			<i>sharp, strong</i> chisel, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				2.607
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
